,title,link,text,language,family
0,Inter-Zab Jewish Neo-Aramaic - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Inter-Zab_Jewish_Neo-Aramaic,"Inter-Zab Jewish Neo-Aramaic, [2][3][4] or Lishanid Noshan, is a modern Jewish-Aramaic dialect, a variant of Northeastern Neo-Aramaic. It was originally spoken in Kurdistan Region of Iraq, in and around Erbil between the Great Zab and Little Zab rivers, it was also spoken in Turkey in the city of Cizre and its environs and in the Hakkari Mountains. Most speakers now live in Israel.",Inter-Zab Jewish Neo-Aramaic,Afro-Asiatic
1,Neo-Aramaic languages - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Neo-Aramaic_languages,"The Neo-Aramaic or Modern Aramaic languages are varieties of Aramaic that evolved during the late medieval and early modern periods, and continue to the present day as vernacular (spoken) languages of modern Aramaic-speaking communities. [1]",Inter-Zab Jewish Neo-Aramaic,Afro-Asiatic
2,Inter-Zab Jewish Neo-Aramaic Explained,https://everything.explained.today/Inter-Zab_Jewish_Neo-Aramaic/,"Inter-Zab Jewish Neo-Aramaic, [2] [3] or Lishanid Noshan, is a modern Jewish-Aramaic dialect, a variant of Northeastern Neo-Aramaic. It was originally spoken in Kurdistan Region of Iraq, in and around Erbil between the Great Zab and Little Zab rivers, it was also spoken in Turkey in the city of Cizre and its environs and in the Hakkari Mountains.",Inter-Zab Jewish Neo-Aramaic,Afro-Asiatic
3,Inter-Zab Jewish Neo-Aramaic - Wikiwand articles,https://www.wikiwand.com/en/articles/Inter-Zab_Jewish_Neo-Aramaic,"Inter-Zab Jewish Neo-Aramaic, [2][3][4] or Lishanid Noshan, is a modern Jewish-Aramaic dialect, a variant of Northeastern Neo-Aramaic. It was originally spoken in Kurdistan Region of Iraq, in and around Arbil between the Great Zab and Little Zab rivers, it was also spoken in Turkey in the city of Cizre and its environs and in the Hakkari Mountains. Most speakers now live in Israel.",Inter-Zab Jewish Neo-Aramaic,Afro-Asiatic
4,Endangered Languages Project - Inter-Zab Jewish Neo-Aramaic,https://elcat.colo.hawaii.edu/lang/3697,"The Jewish Neo-Aramaic dialects, therefore, are approaching extinction. OTHER LANGUAGES USED BY THE COMMUNITY Modern Hebrew; Arabic; Kurdish Modern Hebrew; Arabic; Kurdish LANGUAGE CONTEXT COMMENTS The contacts between the Arabic-speaking Jews and those whose vernacular was Aramaic resulted in a high degree of bilingualism.",Inter-Zab Jewish Neo-Aramaic,Afro-Asiatic
5,Inter-Zab Jewish Neo-Aramaic | Detailed Pedia,https://www.detailedpedia.com/wiki-Inter-Zab_Jewish_Neo-Aramaic,"Inter-Zab Jewish Neo-Aramaic, or Lishanid Noshan, is a modern Jewish-Aramaic dialect, a variant of Northeastern Neo-Aramaic. It was originally spoken in Kurdistan Region of Iraq, in and around Hewler between the Great Zab and Little Zab rivers, it was also spoken in Turkey in the city of Cizre and its environs and in the Hakkari Mountains. Most speakers now live in Israel.",Inter-Zab Jewish Neo-Aramaic,Afro-Asiatic
6,Inter-Zab Jewish Neo-Aramaic language resources | Joshua Project,https://joshuaproject.net/languages/aij,Inter-Zab Jewish Neo-Aramaic language resources. Listing of people groups speaking Inter-Zab Jewish Neo-Aramaic. Inter-Zab Jewish Neo-Aramaic dialects and alternate names. Bible and ministry resource availability.,Inter-Zab Jewish Neo-Aramaic,Afro-Asiatic
7,Inter-Zab Jewish Neo-Aramaic - Wikiwand,https://www.wikiwand.com/en/articles/Lishanid_Noshan,"Inter-Zab Jewish Neo-Aramaic, [2][3][4] or Lishanid Noshan, is a modern Jewish-Aramaic dialect, a variant of Northeastern Neo-Aramaic. It was originally spoken in Kurdistan Region of Iraq, in and around Arbil between the Great Zab and Little Zab rivers, it was also spoken in Turkey in the city of Cizre and its environs and in the Hakkari Mountains. Most speakers now live in Israel.",Inter-Zab Jewish Neo-Aramaic,Afro-Asiatic
8,"שבתה -AFRO JEWISH JAZZ ""shabate / ""music - YouTube",https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=rdohHmbPFyc,A fascinating edgy fusion of Ethiopian Jazz-Afro Rhythm Grooves with traditional Jewish soul. Shabate is one of the most extraordinary statements of contemporary music scene of Israel.,Inter-Zab Jewish Neo-Aramaic,Afro-Asiatic
9,Inter-Zab Jewish Neo-Aramaic Language (AIJ) - Ethnologue,https://www.ethnologue.com/language/aij/,Inter-Zab Jewish Neo-Aramaic is an endangered indigenous language of Israel. It belongs to the Afro-Asiatic language family. The language is used as a first language by older adults only. It is not known to be taught in schools.,Inter-Zab Jewish Neo-Aramaic,Afro-Asiatic
